  "body": "See the explainer: https://github.com/mfreed7/split-tabs for all the details.\n\nRoughly, this adds the ability to open split tabs from `window.open()`, in very much the same way that it can be used to open popup windows. This PR also adds a declarative equivalent (the `windowFeatures` attribute) to `window.open()`'s window features string, allowing declarative access to specify how a URL is opened.\n\nQuick code snippet:\n```html\n<script>\n// Open on the left, taking 30% of the width.\nwindow.open(\"https://www.example.com\", \"_blank\", \"split,splitposition=left,splitsize=30\");\n</script>\n\n<a href=\"https://example.com\" target=\"_blank\"\n   windowfeatures=\"split,splitposition=left,splitsize=30\">Equivalent to above JS code</a>\n```\n\nCloses #13153.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium\n   * …\n- [X] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://wpt.fyi/results/html/browsers/the-window-object/open-close?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=open-features-split\n   * https://wpt.fyi/results/html/browsers/the-window-object/open-close?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=declarative-windowfeatures\n   * … <!-- If these tests are tentative, link a PR to make them non-tentative. -->\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: https://crbug.com/570412924\n   * Gecko: …\n   * WebKit: …\n- [ ] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs:\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: …\n- [X] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/form-control-infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 9:40 PM UTC (beef204)\">/form-control-infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/a044232...beef204/form-control-infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 9:40 PM UTC (beef204)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/forms.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 9:40 PM UTC (beef204)\">/forms.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/a044232...beef204/forms.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 9:40 PM UTC (beef204)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/image-maps.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 9:40 PM UTC (beef204)\">/image-maps.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/a044232...beef204/image-maps.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 9:40 PM UTC (beef204)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 9:40 PM UTC (beef204)\">/indices.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/a044232...beef204/indices.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 9:40 PM UTC (beef204)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/links.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 9:40 PM UTC (beef204)\">/links.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/a044232...beef204/links.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 11, 2026, 9:40 PM UTC (beef204)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13245/nav-hi